  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts`. It typechecks, but I couldn't run `vite build` or view a rendered frame, so how it looks is untested.\n\n- **Island:** the terrain is a flat-shaded heightfield with an irregular coastline. It has sand, grass and rock colouring by height and slope. Pine trees and faceted rocks are merged into one second mesh. Both meshes are built in code with no model files.\n- **Water:** a custom shader on a large wave mesh. The waves are animated and shaded in facets. It has deep and shallow colours, a foam ring that follows the shoreline, sun or moon glints and a fade to the sky colour at the horizon. Its lighting uniforms update every frame.\n- **Day/night:** a 20-second cycle moves the sun across the sky in front of the camera. Each frame it updates the sky, the sun's position, colour and intensity, a moon light opposite the sun, and the hemisphere light. Night keeps a floor of moon and hemisphere light, so the scene shouldn't go black.\n- **Camera:** an orbit camera above the water, framing the island, drifting slowly.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after the scene is ready and two animation frames have passed.\n\nThe camera orbit and per-frame sky and light updates use engine calls I only checked against the type definitions and docs.\n\n",
